"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2025-11-02T13:46:21Z","updated_at":"2025-11-02T13:46:56Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.5.stable.official [876b29033]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.stable - macOS Sequoia (15.6.0) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Metal (Forward+) - integrated Apple M1 Pro (Apple7) - Apple M1 Pro (8 threads) - 16.00 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nThere is a certain unclearness about how thos parameters work and how they affect each others.\nfor reference this si how it looks right now on\n<img width=\"651\" height=\"494\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/56dd5fb5-5961-4119-8315-9083f96f0dfd\" />\n\n\nThere is two part that are unclear to me :\n- It is really unclear which parameters are set or not by the preset\n- Some parameters are uselesss at some points because they are overriden by another parameter and there is nothing indicating that. \n\n\nTo fix the first one I think we should simply restructure the settings to make clear which parameters are set by the preset. I was thinking of something like this :\n<img width=\"700\" height=\"651\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/74c2e907-ffbc-4ef9-929b-8577e3e69d33\" />\n\nto fix the second one I think the best idea would be to at least make them close to the one overriding it. An even better solution would be to make them read-only when they are overriden \n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nN/A\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/11